{
  "case_id": "2008-07-1309",
  "document_hash": "edd2db58f97f59faf8cfca30d906c6683e55685490eea8b9fd039c4abe750e29",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edd2db58f97f59faf8cfca30d906c6683e55685490eea8b9fd039c4abe750e29",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edd2db58f97f-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:16 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Marc Fernich",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edd2db58f97f59faf8cfca30d906c6683e55685490eea8b9fd039c4abe750e29",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edd2db58f97f-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This is a case about a defendant's right to an independent jury determination of each essential element of a RICO offense, specifically a pattern of racketeering and a separate enterprise that is more than just a duplication of the pattern."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edd2db58f97f59faf8cfca30d906c6683e55685490eea8b9fd039c4abe750e29",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edd2db58f97f-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: The -- the error was the failure to give the instruction that appears on page 95 of the joint appendix? Is that the error that you are complaining about?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edd2db58f97f59faf8cfca30d906c6683e55685490eea8b9fd039c4abe750e29",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edd2db58f97f-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What -- what do you mean by that precisely? Suppose you have a group of people, the ringleader goes and gets a safecracker, he gets a wheelman, and so forth, all the people he needs for the crime; and he says we are going to call this the -- the Brinks Job Group, okay? We are the Brinks Job Group."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edd2db58f97f59faf8cfca30d906c6683e55685490eea8b9fd039c4abe750e29",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edd2db58f97f-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, what structure would there be there? What characteristics of that group would satisfy the structural requirement?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. FERNICH",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edd2db58f97f59faf8cfca30d906c6683e55685490eea8b9fd039c4abe750e29",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edd2db58f97f-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FERNICH: The ongoing existence, the regular meetings, and the degree of sophistication employed. And it implies that they are not just sort of getting together on an impromptu basis as opportunities arise, but they are sitting around on a regular basis for a -- a continuing period of time and planning things out."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edd2db58f97f59faf8cfca30d906c6683e55685490eea8b9fd039c4abe750e29",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edd2db58f97f-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: How about during the period that this man -- what was his name, Mangia --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. YANG",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edd2db58f97f59faf8cfca30d906c6683e55685490eea8b9fd039c4abe750e29",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edd2db58f97f-0001-0010",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF ANTHONY YANG ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edd2db58f97f59faf8cfca30d906c6683e55685490eea8b9fd039c4abe750e29",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edd2db58f97f-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: When you say \"individual,\" the first part of the definition of \"enterprise\" speaks about any individual partnership, corporation, association, or other legal entity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edd2db58f97f59faf8cfca30d906c6683e55685490eea8b9fd039c4abe750e29",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edd2db58f97f-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What appendix? Not the joint appendix?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edd2db58f97f59faf8cfca30d906c6683e55685490eea8b9fd039c4abe750e29",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edd2db58f97f-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Would you agree there could be a situation in which an individual engages in a pattern of racketeering activity together with other people and yet is not participating in the affairs of an enterprise through the pattern of racketeering activity?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edd2db58f97f59faf8cfca30d906c6683e55685490eea8b9fd039c4abe750e29",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edd2db58f97f-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Why -- I guess that's where I'm losing the argument. Why is it difficult?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edd2db58f97f59faf8cfca30d906c6683e55685490eea8b9fd039c4abe750e29",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edd2db58f97f-0001-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Before you do that, Mr. Yang, could you give us a sense, if you know it, about the practical results of the different formulas that -- there are at least three formulas, I take it that the different circuits have approved."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edd2db58f97f59faf8cfca30d906c6683e55685490eea8b9fd039c4abe750e29",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edd2db58f97f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: What did you think -- what did you think of the -- probably not much of it, but what did you think of my effort there? And I am trying to point out, as you see, I am open to anything that will deal with what I think of as a functional problem and the functional problem is exhibited by that Posner"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edd2db58f97f59faf8cfca30d906c6683e55685490eea8b9fd039c4abe750e29",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edd2db58f97f-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: I am -- I am really confused now. I don't -- I am not sure I know what your answer to the question presented is, which is quite simply must an association-in-fact enterprise under RICO have some ascertainable structure beyond that inherent in the commission of predicate crimes by its members and associates? And you -- your answer is no?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Yang",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edd2db58f97f59faf8cfca30d906c6683e55685490eea8b9fd039c4abe750e29",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edd2db58f97f-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. YANG: Because Turkette makes very clear that an association-in-fact enterprise can exist for wholly criminal acts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edd2db58f97f59faf8cfca30d906c6683e55685490eea8b9fd039c4abe750e29",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edd2db58f97f-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Where -- where in your briefs or in the materials do we find the definition of what the enterprise is, other than in the statute, other than the terms of the statute itself?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fernich",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "edd2db58f97f59faf8cfca30d906c6683e55685490eea8b9fd039c4abe750e29",
      "evidence_id": "ev-edd2db58f97f-0002-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "we would certainly agree with Justice Breyer's formulation that something to differentiate it as a long-term, goal-directed, decisionmaking apparatus that continues in the intervals between the predicate acts would do it"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1309",
      "confidence": 0.0,
